# text = Her eyes blazed at me , and she tapped the ground impatiently with her foot I asked She spoke in a low , eager voice , with a curious lisp in her utterance she cried Stapleton had abandoned the chase and came back to us breathing hard and flushed with his exertions said he , and it seemed to me that the tone of his greeting was not altogether a cordial one He spoke unconcernedly , but his small light eyes glanced incessantly from the girl to me said I A flush of vexation passed over her expressive face said she her brother remarked with the same questioning eyes said she A short walk brought us to it , a bleak moorland house , once the farm of some grazier in the old prosperous days , but now put into repair and turned into a modern dwelling .
